  "raw_text": "{\n  \"options\": [\n    \"Teens should compare their daily lives with the curated images they see online.\"\n    \"Social media allows people to compare their vacations to those of others.\"\n    \"Comparing themselves to popular posts makes teens feel inadequate.\"\n    \"The survey found that many teens compare their appearance to influencers.\"\n    \"We can compare the negative effects of social media with the benefits.\"\n    \"Teenagers often compare their real lives to the highlights shown on their screens.\"\n    \"Social media encourages a constant comparison of one's own life to others.\"\n    \"We should compare the advantages of social media with its drawbacks.\"\n    \"Looking at others' posts is a form of comparison that harms self-esteem.\"\n    \"Teens should compare their self-image to the best moments posted by others.\"\n    \"This comparison leads to feelings of badness about their own lives.\"\n    \"We can compare the time spent on social media with the time spent with friends.\"\n    \"The survey suggests that almost half of teens compare themselves to others.\"\n    \"Comparing oneself to the best parts of others' lives is a common habit.\"\n    \"Teens should compare their real lives to the edited versions they see.\"\n    \"Social media makes people compare their lives to the perfect lives of others.\"\n    \"Comparing oneself to others causes teens to feel bad about their own lives.\"\n    \"We should compare the negative effects of social media with its positive uses.\"\n    \"Teens often compare their current lives to the vacations and clothes they post.\"\n    \"This constant comparison leads to feelings of inadequacy.\"\n    \"We can compare the time spent on social media with the time spent with friends.\"\n    \"Teens should compare their self-image to the best moments posted by others.\"\n    \"Social media encourages a comparison of one's own life to others' experiences.\"\n    \"The survey found that many teens com